[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186184229 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" "question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" "question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" "question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184143 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" "question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" "question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" "question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/id #uuid "43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119592" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}-b\\sqrt{14}}{8},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{8}+\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}-1\\sqrt{14}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,b=1,$ and $a+b=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" "answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" "answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" "answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" "answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" :answer/id #uuid "8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" :answer/id #uuid "b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer/id #uuid "6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" :answer/id #uuid "bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b" :answer/id #uuid "3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/id #uuid "1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-325842" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{7}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{24}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that both $u$ and $v$ lie in the first quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} $\\sqrt{3}\\,+\\,$ {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $50$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive, we take\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{24}{25})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{7}{25})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}}{50}+\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}+7}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" "answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/id #uuid "96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/id #uuid "39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/id #uuid "1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119581" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}-b}{26},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(-\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{12}{13})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{26}+\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}}{26} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}-5}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=12,b=5,$ and $a+b=17.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" "answer-d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d" "answer-4692ff53-10f8-5d92-a62c-7ea8c8eb0b75" "answer-a82aa644-63bf-5607-827a-5038ebc9e460" "answer-85e69bf9-0ffa-5440-9692-3b79b4593ab1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/id #uuid "9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d" :answer/id #uuid "d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4692ff53-10f8-5d92-a62c-7ea8c8eb0b75" :answer/id #uuid "4692ff53-10f8-5d92-a62c-7ea8c8eb0b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a82aa644-63bf-5607-827a-5038ebc9e460" :answer/id #uuid "a82aa644-63bf-5607-827a-5038ebc9e460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85e69bf9-0ffa-5440-9692-3b79b4593ab1" :answer/id #uuid "85e69bf9-0ffa-5440-9692-3b79b4593ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/id #uuid "97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/math-academy-id "q-143842" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{4}{5},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{4}{5})(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{15}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+8\\sqrt{2}}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" "answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" "answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" "answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" "answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" :answer/id #uuid "41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer/id #uuid "2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3+8\\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" :answer/id #uuid "53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3-8\\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" :answer/id #uuid "d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4+6\\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36" :answer/id #uuid "01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4-6\\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/id #uuid "3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/math-academy-id "q-141440" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{5}{13}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{7}-b\\sqrt{2}}{39},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})-(-\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{39}+\\frac{5\\sqrt{7}}{39} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{7}-12\\sqrt{2}}{39}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=5,b=12,$ and $a+b=17.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-831aaab2-d476-5739-b94e-9e3263993fc7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-831aaab2-d476-5739-b94e-9e3263993fc7" :answer-field/id #uuid "831aaab2-d476-5739-b94e-9e3263993fc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" "answer-295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" "answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" "answer-216e442c-c072-5728-a705-afb102d6fbea" "answer-285237b4-7d17-5283-a8ae-a41635f56b71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" :answer/id #uuid "14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" :answer/id #uuid "295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer/id #uuid "a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-216e442c-c072-5728-a705-afb102d6fbea" :answer/id #uuid "216e442c-c072-5728-a705-afb102d6fbea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-285237b4-7d17-5283-a8ae-a41635f56b71" :answer/id #uuid "285237b4-7d17-5283-a8ae-a41635f56b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" :question/id #uuid "9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" :question/math-academy-id "q-325885" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{26}-\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{26} \\\\  & =-\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/id #uuid "b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer/id #uuid "ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{26}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/id #uuid "50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/math-academy-id "q-141443" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}+b\\sqrt{5}}{20},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})-(\\frac{1}{4})(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{20}+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}+2\\sqrt{5}}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=5,b=2,$ and $a+b=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/id #uuid "77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" "answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" "answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" "answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" "answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" :answer/id #uuid "13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" :answer/id #uuid "321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" :answer/id #uuid "367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer/id #uuid "c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4" :answer/id #uuid "5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184540 :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{24}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{7}{25},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{25})(-\\frac{4}{5})+(-\\frac{24}{25})(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{125}-\\frac{72}{125} \\\\  & =-\\frac{44}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186181416 :answer-field/correct 17592186181421 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/id #uuid "77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-141441" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{7},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=-\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}+b}{14},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{7})(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{14}-\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{14} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}+5}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=6,b=5,$ and $a+b=11.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de040dcd-65e4-5530-8e4b-808b33262dec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de040dcd-65e4-5530-8e4b-808b33262dec" :answer-field/id #uuid "de040dcd-65e4-5530-8e4b-808b33262dec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" "answer-f696b631-7dc2-5a31-af20-dff99b948f2c" "answer-936f28df-a16a-538a-be6a-eec59f948467" "answer-e76101c8-badb-5987-9480-28be10e44a22" "answer-7fd779df-49e5-5e25-be2d-c22bba641aa2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer/id #uuid "8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f696b631-7dc2-5a31-af20-dff99b948f2c" :answer/id #uuid "f696b631-7dc2-5a31-af20-dff99b948f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-936f28df-a16a-538a-be6a-eec59f948467" :answer/id #uuid "936f28df-a16a-538a-be6a-eec59f948467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e76101c8-badb-5987-9480-28be10e44a22" :answer/id #uuid "e76101c8-badb-5987-9480-28be10e44a22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fd779df-49e5-5e25-be2d-c22bba641aa2" :answer/id #uuid "7fd779df-49e5-5e25-be2d-c22bba641aa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185350 :tutorial/content "We can compute trigonometric ratios using the sum and difference formulas for cosine together with the Pythagorean identity.\n\nLet's suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin u = \\dfrac{1}{3}, \\qquad\n\\sin v = \\dfrac {3}{5}, \\qquad\n\\cos v = -\\dfrac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nHow can we find the value of $\\cos\\left(u - v\\right)$ given that $u$ lies in the second quadrant?\n\nFirst, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{u}$, $\\sin{v}$, and $\\cos{v}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{u}$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 u + \\cos^2 u = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 u = 1- \\sin^2 u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\cos u= -\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cos(u - v) \n\t\t\t&= \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\left( -\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\right) \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right) +  \\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right) \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right) \\[5pt]\t\t\t\n \t\t\t&= \\dfrac{8\\sqrt{2}}{15} + \\dfrac{3}{15} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{8\\sqrt{2}+3}{15}\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184424 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/id #uuid "43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e"] ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119592"] ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}-b\\sqrt{14}}{8},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{8}+\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}-1\\sqrt{14}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,b=1,$ and $a+b=4.$"] ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb"] ["answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" :answer/id #uuid "8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908"] ["answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" :answer/id #uuid "b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf"] ["answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer/id #uuid "6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69"] ["answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" :answer/id #uuid "bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07"] ["answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07" :answer/value "7"] ["answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b" :answer/id #uuid "3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b"] ["answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b" :answer/value "9"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/correct "answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-8d53cd2a-8bc8-5203-a4b8-0c7848792908"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-b87397f3-ec91-5023-b6e1-c9d09c5dfccf"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ddca841-e0d9-56b3-8b19-47941defcf69"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-bfd58ea1-aff0-5d22-8f67-8c8bb8e6db07"] ["answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb" :answer-field/choices "answer-3e66c7b2-03cf-5b40-acd9-587dadb9ac9b"] ["question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-afbfba15-89cd-5f8b-8d11-e527ad3d57cb"] [17592186184229 :knowledge-point/questions "question-43bdc32f-8f5e-5fac-84f7-776394b1cc9e"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/id #uuid "1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-325842"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{7}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{24}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that both $u$ and $v$ lie in the first quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} $\\sqrt{3}\\,+\\,$ {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $50$ |"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive, we take\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{24}{25})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{7}{25})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}}{50}+\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\sqrt{3}+7}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f"] ["answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/id #uuid "96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c"] ["answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c" :answer/value "24"] ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/correct "answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c"] ["answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f" :answer-field/choices "answer-96a9999f-2cfe-5e9a-9d15-879182a3d07c"] ["answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a"] ["answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/id #uuid "39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7"] ["answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7" :answer/value "7"] ["answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/correct "answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7"] ["answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a" :answer-field/choices "answer-39ef944c-140e-545c-9889-fb5a89c666b7"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3710dd2a-0992-5c4b-b6c5-20c3ea7c9d8f"] ["question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-43029c72-41de-531d-9dff-6296500d2b7a"] [17592186184229 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1059df0b-e279-5183-9a0b-f6c9c0f186a7"] ["question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/id #uuid "1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f"] ["question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119581"] ["question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}-b}{26},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(-\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{12}{13})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{26}+\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}}{26} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\sqrt{3}-5}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=12,b=5,$ and $a+b=17.$"] ["question-1ed725f0-66d2-5a2d-ad80-26e42df0423f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4db31d4f-92dd-5a4c-a9aa-c0b389b1913c"] ["answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/id #uuid "9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede"] ["answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f2fef72-fcfd-58d8-bc85-22f6495c4ede" :answer/value "17"] ["answer-d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d" :answer/id #uuid "d741e5c8-f214-5380-b086-fc6bdd2df65d"] ["answer-d741e5c8-f214-