"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/id #uuid "97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/math-academy-id "q-143842"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{4}{5},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v).$"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{4}{5})(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{15}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+8\\sqrt{2}}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3"] ["answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" :answer/id #uuid "41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1"] ["answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1" :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{2}}{15}"] ["answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer/id #uuid "2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb"] ["answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb" :answer/value "\\frac{3+8\\sqrt{2}}{15}"] ["answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" :answer/id #uuid "53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a"] ["answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a" :answer/value "\\frac{3-8\\sqrt{2}}{15}"] ["answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" :answer/id #uuid "d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806"] ["answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806" :answer/value "\\frac{4+6\\sqrt{2}}{15}"] ["answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36" :answer/id #uuid "01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36"] ["answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36" :answer/value "\\frac{4-6\\sqrt{2}}{15}"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/correct "answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-41b89c7d-25df-5525-b5cb-ba7faba112c1"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-2b869f32-d6ca-57fc-b45e-d252c7e98fbb"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-53b3b239-af76-5af9-8ec7-54d956c4236a"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-d5703300-df93-5e24-bec4-819d88120806"] ["answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-01664bcb-25bc-5604-ac5b-7905582c2b36"] ["question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a3e78b0b-13cf-51a9-87c2-6116b81037d3"] [17592186184229 :knowledge-point/questions "question-97e789b8-dcb1-527a-b969-3a0ccc1e1111"] ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/id #uuid "3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681"] ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/math-academy-id "q-141440"] ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{5}{13}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{7}-b\\sqrt{2}}{39},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})-(-\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{39}+\\frac{5\\sqrt{7}}{39} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{7}-12\\sqrt{2}}{39}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=5,b=12,$ and $a+b=17.$"] ["question-3f0420a1-666b-5191-842f-3d2bdb44e681" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-831aaab2-d476-5739-b94e-9e3263993fc7" :answer-field/id #uuid "831aaab2-d476-5739-b94e-9e3263993fc7"] ["answer-14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" :answer/id #uuid "14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e"] ["answer-14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-14aab469-1f71-5582-a61c-34ca084d5f6e" :answer/value "11"] ["answer-295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" :answer/id #uuid "295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad"] ["answer-295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-295f06f2-f22f-5444-b217-5a8a03ad09ad" :answer/value "13"] ["answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer/id #uuid "a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa"] ["answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a3d3096c-e5b3-55c4-80ea-469e433551fa" :answer/value "17"] ["answer-216e442c-c072-5728-a705-afb102d6fbea" :answer/id #uuid "216e442c-c072-5728-a705-afb102d