 $u$ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}."] ["question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{25}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{26}-\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{26} \\\\  & =-\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/id #uuid "b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48"] ["answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer/id #uuid "ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6"] ["answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6" :answer/value "-\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{26}"] ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/correct "answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6"] ["answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48" :answer-field/choices "answer-ee7a38c5-9093-561e-b5af-54b8e86b60c6"] ["question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b69a755b-9199-59fe-b15b-6dc54413bd48"] [17592186184143 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9e4e39a8-9ee3-514c-8a99-c8c4e6788313"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/id #uuid "50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/math-academy-id "q-141443"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}+b\\sqrt{5}}{20},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})-(\\frac{1}{4})(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{20}+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}+2\\sqrt{5}}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=5,b=2,$ and $a+b=7.$"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/id #uuid "77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604"] ["answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" :answer/id #uuid "13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703"] ["answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703" :answer/value "11"] ["answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" :answer/id #uuid "321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41"] ["answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41" :answer/value "13"] ["answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" :answer/id #uuid "367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a"] ["answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer/id #uuid "c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168"] ["answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168" :answer/value "7"] ["answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4" :answer/id #uuid "5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4"] ["answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4" :answer/value "9"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/correct "answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/choices "answer-13e18065-a00c-590c-bd30-b3697aef1703"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/choices "answer-321078fd-ddc7-5fa9-8ffd-02d0df3acd41"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/choices "answer-367fba42-a7e2-593f-bdf2-3db31fe9789a"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/choices "answer-c88bd8a5-d479-58a6-8d0c-28fb55f5c168"] ["answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604" :answer-field/choices "answer-5b80064a-5abe-5355-884e-5d229396f3a4"] ["question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-77b4248f-fe82-5a6e-b664-fd773a876604"] [17592186184143 :knowledge-point/questions "question-50ab1b1c-89b6-5bde-a50d-34d9fce11246"] [17592186184540 :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{24}{25},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{7}{25},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v).$"] [17592186184540 :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{25})(-\\frac{4}{5})+(-\\frac{24}{25})(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{125}-\\frac{72}{125} \\\\  & =-\\frac{44}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186184540 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186181416 :answer-field/correct 17592186181421] ["question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/id #uuid "77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9"] ["question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-141441"] ["question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{7},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=-\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}+b}{14},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,$ $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{7})(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{14}-\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{14} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}+5}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=6,b=5,$ and $a+b=11.$"] ["question-77e70b3f-8704-511e-87c9-d67cfcbe9ec9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-de040dcd-65e4-5530-8e4b-808b33262dec" :answer-field/id #uuid "de040dcd-65e4-5530-8e4b-808b33262dec"] ["answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer/id #uuid "8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf"] ["answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8b795d79-1d06-5f11-b31e-dc17f7053fbf" :answer/value "11"] ["answer-f696b631-7dc2-5a31-af20-dff99b948f2c" :answer/id #uuid "f696b631-7dc2-5a31-af20